.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.\" Title
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.TH OMSimulator 1 "" "OpenModelica @OM_MANPAGE_VERSION@" "OpenModelica User Commands"
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH NAME
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
OMSimulator \- simulate an FMU or an SSP system
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.B OMSimulator
.RI [ options ]
.I model
.br
.B OMSimulator
.B \-\-validate
.I model
.br
.B OMSimulator
.I script.py
.RI [ arguments ]
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.B OMSimulator
simulates a
.I model
given as an FMU
.RI ( .fmu )
or an SSP system structure
.RI ( .ssp ),
without a Modelica compiler and without writing a driver script.
.PP
The simulation settings \(em start and stop time, result file, tolerance and
the rest \(em are taken from the model itself. The options below override
them.
.PP
The file is validated against its schema, FMI for
.IR .fmu ,
SSP for
.IR .ssp ,
before it is simulated. With
.B \-\-validate
it is only validated and not simulated.
.PP
Given a
.I script.py
instead, it runs the Python driver script with the OMSimulator Python module
on its path, passing on the
.IR arguments .
.PP
.B OMSimulator
is also available as a library with C and Python bindings; this page describes
only the command line program.
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH OPTIONS
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
Every
.BI \-\- flag
that switches something on has a
.BI \-\-no\- flag
counterpart that switches it off.
.
.SS "General"
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-validate
Only validate the file against its schema; do not simulate.
.TP
.B \-\-clearAllOptions
Reset every flag to its default.
.TP
.BI \-\-logFile " file"
Write the log to
.IR file .
The default is standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-logLevel " n"
0 for the default, 1 to add debug messages, 2 to add traces.
.TP
.B \-\-progressBar
Show the simulation progress in the terminal. Off by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
Give up after
.I seconds
of simulation. 0, the default, disables the limit.
.TP
.BI \-\-numProcs " n"
Use at most
.I n
processors; 0 chooses automatically. The default is 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-tempDir " directory"
Where temporary files are written. The default is the working directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-workingDir " directory"
The working directory. The default is the current one.
.TP
.B \-\-deleteTempFiles
Delete temporary files as soon as they are no longer needed. On by default.
.TP
.B \-\-suppressPath
Leave path information out of info messages, which makes output comparable
between machines. On by default.
.
.SS "Time and steps"
.TP
.BI \-\-startTime " time"
.TQ
.BI \-\-stopTime " time"
Override the interval the model asks for.
.TP
.BI \-\-stepSize " size"
The (maximum) step size. FMUs only; the default comes from the model.
.TP
.BI \-\-initialStepSize " size"
The first step size. The default is 1e\-06.
.TP
.BI \-\-minimumStepSize " size"
The smallest step size. The default is 1e\-12.
.TP
.BI \-\-intervals " n"
The number of communication points, greater than 1. The default is 500.
.TP
.BI \-\-tolerance " tol"
The relative tolerance. The default comes from the model.
.TP
.B \-\-realTime
Experimental soft real-time co-simulation. Off by default.
.
.SS "Solvers"
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " cs" \fR|\fP \fIme\fP
Force co-simulation or model exchange for an FMU that exports both. The
default is co-simulation.
.TP
.BI \-\-solver " euler" \fR|\fP \fIcvode\fP
The ODE solver for model-exchange FMUs. The default is cvode.
.TP
.BI \-\-master " algorithm"
The master algorithm. The default is
.BR ma .
.TP
.BI \-\-algLoopSolver " fixedpoint" \fR|\fP \fIkinsol\fP
How algebraic loops spanning several components are solved. The default is
kinsol.
.TP
.BI \-\-maxLoopIteration " n"
The iteration limit for those loops; loops inside a component are unaffected.
The default is 10.
.TP
.BI \-\-maxEventIteration " n"
The iteration limit for handling one event. The default is 100.
.TP
.B \-\-directionalDerivatives
Use directional derivatives for the algebraic loop Jacobian. On by default.
.TP
.B \-\-emitEvents
Emit events during the simulation. On by default.
.TP
.B \-\-inputExtrapolation
Extrapolate inputs using derivative information. Off by default.
.TP
.B \-\-dumpAlgLoops
Dump information about algebraic loops. Off by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-CVODEMaxSteps " n"
.TQ
.BI \-\-CVODEMaxErrTestFails " n"
.TQ
.BI \-\-CVODEMaxNLSIterations " n"
.TQ
.BI \-\-CVODEMaxNLSFailures " n"
CVODE limits: steps (1000), error test failures (100), nonlinear solver
iterations (5) and nonlinear convergence failures (100).
.
.SS "Results"
.TP
.BI \-\-resultFile " file"
Where results are written. The default is the model name with
.B _res.mat
appended.
.TP
.B \-\-stripRoot
Drop the
.B model.root
prefix from exported signal names. Off by default.
.TP
.B \-\-addParametersToCSV
Also write the parameters to a
.B .csv
file. Off by default.
.TP
.B \-\-skipCSVHeader
Leave the delimiter row out of the header of
.B .csv
results. On by default.
.TP
.B \-\-solverStats
Add solver statistics, such as the step size, to the result file. Not every
solver supports it. Off by default.
.TP
.B \-\-wallTime
Add wall clock time to the result file. Off by default.
.
.SS "Tolerating broken FMUs"
.TP
.B \-\-ignoreInitialUnknowns
Ignore the initial unknowns declared in
.BR modelDescription.xml .
Off by default.
.TP
.B \-\-zeroNominal
Accept invalid nominal values, replacing them with 1.0. Off by default.
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH EXAMPLES
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
Simulate an SSP system with the settings it carries:
.PP
.RS
.B OMSimulator test.ssp
.RE
.PP
Check that an FMU is valid without simulating it:
.PP
.RS
.B OMSimulator \-\-validate model.fmu
.RE
.PP
Simulate an FMU as model exchange, to 10 seconds, into a named result file:
.PP
.RS
.B OMSimulator \-\-mode me \-\-stopTime 10 \-\-resultFile out.mat model.fmu
.RE
.
